{
  "fromId": "s",
  "toId": "h",
  "preamble": "Debuccalization of the voiceless alveolar fricative [s] to the glottal fricative [h] removes the oral constriction and leaves only glottal friction. It is one of the most frequent consonant lenitions: it defines the Iranian branch (*saptá > hapta), Ancient Greek (heptá vs Latin septem), Brythonic Celtic (Welsh hen vs Irish sean), Eastern Polynesian (hina vs Samoan sina), Buryat within Mongolic (hara 'moon'), and Igala within Yoruboid (hì 'cook'). In Quechuan, Proto-Quechuan *s became h in 'one' (*suk > huk) in several Quechua I varieties and in Ayacucho and Cuzco Quechua.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Debuccalization, Lenition",
  "languageExamples": [
    {
      "language": "Proto-Iranian / Avestan, Persian",
      "languageFamily": "Iranian",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "Proto-Indo-Iranian *saptá 'seven'",
          "to": "Proto-Iranian *haptá > Avestan hapta, Persian haft",
          "note": "Iranian debuccalized *s to *h except after *k, *n, *p, *t or before *t; Sanskrit keeps saptá."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Proto-Celtic to Welsh",
      "languageFamily": "Brythonic",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "*senos 'old'",
          "to": "hen",
          "note": "Regular initial *s- > h- before vowels in Brythonic; cf. Irish sean"
        },
        {
          "from": "*salanos 'salt'",
          "to": "halen",
          "note": "cf. Irish salann"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Proto-Polynesian to Hawaiian / Māori",
      "languageFamily": "Polynesian",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "*sina 'grey-haired'",
          "to": "Hawaiian, Māori hina",
          "note": "Eastern Polynesian *s > h; Samoan keeps sina"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Proto-Indo-European to Ancient Greek",
      "languageFamily": "Hellenic",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "*septḿ̥ 'seven'",
          "to": "heptá (ἑπτά)",
          "note": "Initial prevocalic *s debuccalized to h (spiritus asper); cf. Latin septem"
        },
        {
          "from": "*seh₂l- 'salt'",
          "to": "háls (ἅλς)",
          "note": "cf. Latin sāl"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Proto-Yoruboid to Igala",
      "languageFamily": "Yoruboid",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "*sì 'to cook'",
          "to": "hì",
          "note": "cf. Yoruba sè, dialectal hè"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Huaylas, Huánuco and Pacaraos Quechua",
      "languageFamily": "Quechua I",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "Proto-Quechuan *suk 'one'",
          "to": "huk",
          "note": "Huaylas, Huánuco and Pacaraos all have huk; Huanca has both huk and suk."
        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-Quechuan *suqta 'six'",
          "to": "Huaylas huqta, Pacaraos huχta",
          "note": "Huánuco suχta and Huanca suʔta keep the sibilant in this word."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Ayacucho and Cuzco Quechua",
      "languageFamily": "Quechua II-C",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "Proto-Quechuan *suk 'one'",
          "to": "Ayacucho huk, Cuzco hux",
          "note": "Cajamarca suχ, Imbabura ʃux and Santiagueño suk keep a sibilant; Cuzco also spirantizes the final stop."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Proto-Oti-Volta to Nawdm",
      "languageFamily": "Yom-Nawdm",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "POV *sôƴm-gá 'hare'",
          "to": "Nawdm hɔ́mgá",
          "note": "Forms in Eddyshaw's transcription: j = [ɟ], y = [j], ɩ ʋ = [ɪ ʊ], a tilde below a vowel marks nasalization, ' marks a glottalized vowel; POV = Proto-Oti-Volta; the final syllable of nouns is a noun-class suffix. Kusaal sú'oŋā and Mooré sóaambà keep s."
        },
        {
          "from": "POV *sṵ́r-fʊ́ 'navel'",
          "to": "Nawdm hírgá",
          "note": "Yom keeps s (sə̄rɣà)."
        },
        {
          "from": "POV *sḛ́r- 'sew'",
          "to": "Nawdm hɔr-"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Proto-Oti-Volta to Nateni",
      "languageFamily": "Eastern Oti-Volta",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "POV *sṵ́r-fʊ́ 'navel'",
          "to": "Nateni hṵ́fā",
          "note": "Mbelime keeps s (sūdìfɛ̀); Ditammari also has h (háá 'dance')."
        },
        {
          "from": "POV *sôƴm-gá 'hare'",
          "to": "Nateni hòǹhī (pl)",
          "note": "Eddyshaw: POV *s > h or zero in Gurma, Nawdm and Ditammari/Nateni, s elsewhere."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Buduma (Kotoko Island)",
      "languageFamily": "Central Chadic",
      "examples": [
